From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 09:41:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] msm8996-common: offer mobile data during setup

A freshly wiped phone reaches the setup wizard with the radio down and no page
offering to turn it on, so on a GApps build the wizard asks you to sign in with
no way online except Wi-Fi, and mobile data has to be switched on by hand after
first reaching the home screen.

That is not a device fault: DataSettingsManager.isProvisioningDataEnabled()
gates data on ro.com.android.prov_mobiledata while DEVICE_PROVISIONED is 0, and
the property defaults to "false". ro.com.android.mobiledata, the old post-setup
switch, no longer exists on 24.0.

Set with PRODUCT_PROPERTY_OVERRIDES, not the PRODUCT_PRODUCT_OVERRIDES two lines
below it -- that is not a build variable, so everything assigned to it is
dropped without a word. The block_binder prop under it only reaches the image
because ims.mk sets it a second time, correctly. Worth knowing before copying
the surrounding style, which is how this nearly shipped doing nothing.

---
 vendor_prop.mk | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/vendor_prop.mk b/vendor_prop.mk
index 402dbc24..a64ad2db 100644
--- a/vendor_prop.mk
+++ b/vendor_prop.mk
@@ -148,6 +148,18 @@ PRODUCT_PROPERTY_OVERRIDES += \
     ro.hwui.text_large_cache_width=3072 \
     ro.hwui.text_large_cache_height=2048
 
+# Mobile data during setup. DataSettingsManager.isProvisioningDataEnabled() gates data on
+# ro.com.android.prov_mobiledata while DEVICE_PROVISIONED is 0, and it defaults to "false" -- so a
+# freshly wiped phone reaches the setup wizard with the radio down and no page offering to turn it
+# on. On a GApps build that is the wizard asking you to sign in with no way to get online except
+# Wi-Fi. (ro.com.android.mobiledata, the old post-setup switch, no longer exists on 24.0.)
+#
+# PRODUCT_PROPERTY_OVERRIDES, not the PRODUCT_PRODUCT_OVERRIDES used just below: that name is not a
+# build variable at all, so everything assigned to it is silently dropped. The block_binder prop
+# below only reaches the image because ims.mk sets it again, correctly.
+PRODUCT_PROPERTY_OVERRIDES += \
+    ro.com.android.prov_mobiledata=true
+
 # IMS
 PRODUCT_PRODUCT_OVERRIDES += \
     ro.telephony.block_binder_thread_on_incoming_calls=false
